course: dictionary
lesson: 16082
title: Waning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe something getting smaller or weaker bit by bit. Waning is one of them. Wane is the base word, and waning is its -ing form, so it tells you the change is happening now. «The moon was waning, so each night it looked a little smaller.» Waning means getting smaller or weaker little by little.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «As the night went on, the light from the lamp was waning.» Night is coming and the light is getting dimmer, so waning must mean fading. Ask yourself: is it growing or shrinking? If it is shrinking, waning fits.
explain: Waning also works for feelings and energy. «Her interest in the game was waning, so she went to read instead.» Her interest was getting weaker, so it was slowly fading away. Something that is on the wane is going down, not up.
fact: Waning means getting smaller or weaker little by little.
fact: The waning moon is the part of the moon's cycle after the full moon, when the lit part we see gets smaller each night.
fact: The opposite of waning is «waxing», which means growing.
fact: Interest, light, strength or energy that is waning is slowly fading away.
fact: Check a new word by swapping in your meaning: «The light was getting smaller» still makes sense, so waning means shrinking or fading.
exercise: «The moon was waning, so each night it looked a little smaller.» What does waning mean? | *Getting smaller bit by bit | Turning a bright shade of blue | Falling out of the sky | Getting brighter very fast
exercise: Holly's energy was waning after the long day at school. What does waning suggest? | *Slowly running out | Fixed in place forever | Sparkling like a star | Growing stronger and stronger
exercise: Which word means the opposite of waning, growing bigger little by little? | Fading | Dimming | Shrinking | *Waxing
test: «Dusk came, and the waning light made it hard to read.» What is the waning light doing? | *Getting weaker little by little | Turning into a rainbow | Getting brighter | Standing still
test: Ravi says, «My interest in the show is waning.» What is he telling us? | He has lost his watch | *His interest is slowly fading | His interest has jumped to the top | His interest is growing fast
exam: Which sentence uses waning correctly? | The waning moon grew bigger every night | Waning means very loud and fast | Waning is a kind of food | *The waning moon looked a little smaller each night
